# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# FraternityOS / Treasury — environment
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit real secrets.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# HOW api/db.py PICKS A CLIENT  (api/config.py: use_local_db == bool(DATABASE_URL))
#   • DATABASE_URL set   → psycopg shim (api/postgres_client.py) talks straight to
#                          that Postgres. Auth treats the JWT `sub` as members.id
#                          (the app's own email+JWT login). RLS is bypassed.
#   • DATABASE_URL empty
#     + SUPABASE_URL set  → supabase-py over PostgREST. Auth treats the JWT `sub`
#                          as members.auth_id (real Supabase Auth users).
#
# For a Supabase DEMO you just create tables in and log into with the app's own
# login, the FIRST mode is by far the simplest: point DATABASE_URL at the Supabase
# connection pooler. You get the demo DB AND the app's email/JWT login, and the
# migrate script + treasury tests already use this same direct connection.
#
# ── MODE A — SUPABASE DEMO (recommended) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase Dashboard → Connect → "Connection pooling" → Session mode.
# IMPORTANT: use the POOLER host (aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com, IPv4).
# The legacy direct host (db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432) is IPv6-only and will fail
# with "Network is unreachable" on IPv4-only networks.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<db-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# Supabase API creds — only needed for MODE B (PostgREST). Harmless to fill in.
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API.
SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon-public-key>
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service-role-key>

# Used by scripts/migrate_db.py and tests/treasury/conftest.py for raw SQL / RPC /
# trigger tests. Point at the SAME pooler URL as DATABASE_URL above (or leave the
# tests to fall back to it). Superuser; bypasses RLS by design.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<db-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# ── MODE B — PostgREST instead of direct Postgres (optional) ─────────────────
# Leave DATABASE_URL EMPTY and rely on SUPABASE_URL + keys above. Requires real
# Supabase Auth users (members.auth_id populated) — more setup than Mode A.

# ── MODE C — fully offline local Docker Postgres ─────────────────────────────
# `USE_DOCKER_DB=1 bash deploy/local-dev.sh`, then:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://fraternityos:localdev@localhost:5434/fraternityos

# ── App ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
JWT_SECRET=local-dev-secret-key-change-in-prod
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001
CHECKIN_LINK_TTL_MINUTES=10

# Shared secret for the Vercel Cron caller (/api/cron/process-fines). Empty → the
# endpoint returns 401 (disabled). In Vercel, set CRON_SECRET and the platform
# sends it as `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` automatically.
CRON_SECRET=

# Feature development flags
FEATURE_VP_OPERATIONS=1
FEATURE_SECRETARY_COMMS=1

# Secretary / Treasury messaging — dry_run persists outbox rows but sends nothing.
MESSAGE_DELIVERY_MODE=dry_run
ESCALATION_DELAY_MINUTES=120
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_FROM_PHONE=
SENDGRID_API_KEY=
SENDGRID_FROM_EMAIL=
MESSAGE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=local-webhook-secret-change-in-prod
